  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch16-03> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch16-03--gpt> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch16-03--gpt> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "GPT-5.6 Sol on thompson1917-ch16-03: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.68" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.682"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.78"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Hollowness and bending efficiency are measurable, but “where required” risks selecting cases by the outcome. Open scans support broad comparative tests, though functional loading and full taxonomic coverage remain incomplete." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Quantify cross-sectional hollowness and second moment of area in structures exposed to multidirectional bending, comparing them with structures under other dominant loads while controlling size. Frequent solid cores in the target class would refute the generalization." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Loading regime is not encoded with most scans.", "The scope combines nonhomologous animal and plant structures." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch16-03--gpt--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch16-03--gpt--dataset-2> .
